<Base title="Harness² Lab research archive" description="Agent optimization research, validation evidence, and instructions for running the Harness² simulator locally.">
  <article class="container page-shell project-detail">
    <a class="text-link" href="/projects/recursa/#agent-optimization">← Recursa Studio</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Harness² Lab research archive</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Harness² studies how an agent can propose, probe, and compose changes to the prompts, rules, memory, and tools around a frozen model. The hosted runtime is retired. The simulator, Budget Lab, and optional model backends remain available in the source for local use.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Run the simulator locally</h2>
        <p>Use the pinned release and follow its setup instructions. The scripted simulator runs without a provider account or API key.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={source + '#quick-start'}>Setup instructions and source</a></li>
          <li><a href={source + '/app/static'}>Interactive lab source</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Evidence and attribution</h2>
        <p>The release includes nine synthetic tasks, automated checks, and simulated adaptive compute results. Those results describe simulator behavior. Model-backed improvement requires separate measurements.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={source + '/data/budget_lab.json'}>Recorded simulator data</a></li>
          <li><a href={source + '/tests'}>Validation tests</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14224">Read the Harness² paper</a></li>
          <li><a href="/harness2-lab/LICENSE">Lab license</a> · <a href="/harness2-lab/NOTICE">Lab notice</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
